abstract: >-
  A CPU-only, real-time system that classifies head direction as front, left or right from a
  single webcam frame, developed for online-assessment integrity and driver-attention
  monitoring. On a dataset of 400 photographs of three subjects, a two-parameter geometric
  estimator derived from MediaPipe Face Mesh landmarks reaches 95.06% on a held-out split and
  94.75% +/- 1.66% under 5-fold cross-validation, outperforming a fine-tuned EfficientNetB0
  (80.25%) by 15 points while running 13 times faster at 174 FPS on a desktop CPU. The
  geometric score is invariant to input resolution from 512 px down to 128 px, whereas the
  CNN loses 17 points over the same range. Under a leave-one-subject-out protocol accuracy
  falls to 87.49% +/- 10.98%, which the repository reports as the honest operating point;
  threshold transfer, not landmark detection, is the measured failure mode.
